/ActualText (Don't Overcrowd Slides: Avoid filling slides with excessive content. Keep the text concise and use bullet points or short phrases to convey information. Leave ample white space to maintain a clean and uncluttered look.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Stick with One Theme: Choose a consistent theme or template for your slides. This ensures a cohesive and professional appearance throughout your presentation. Use the same font, colors, and graphical elements across all slides.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Limit the Number of Colors: Stick to a limited color palette to maintain visual harmony and prevent distractions. Select a few colors that complement each other and use them consistently throughout your slides.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Use Animations and Graphics: Incorporate tasteful animations and relevant graphics to add visual interest to your slides. Animations can help emphasize key points or transition between sections smoothly. Graphics such as icons, charts, or images can enhance understanding and engagement.)
